/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (2.1 Introduction)
/E (2.1 Introduction)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( In this chapter, we will discuss the needs of the current accounting system used by Al Nahda Foundation. This assessment includes defining the problem, conducting a gap analysis, and describing the project scope. It then goes on to analyze the challenges, identify objectives, and identify key requirements for improvement. One of the most prominent systems currently deployed in the retail sector is the New Point accounting system. However, operations management faces many challenges in communicating with suppliers and processing purchases efficiently. The process remains manual and time-consuming, potentially leading to delays. This delay leads to increased errors and, consequently, decreased productivity.At the beginning of the chapter, the main problems facing the current system and their causes are explained. After that, the objectives and constraints related to development and improvement are clarified. Then, the gap analysis is presented in a table that shows the most important differences between the current situation and the future situation. Finally, this chapter will define the scope of the project and the stakeholders associated with it.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
298 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (2.2 Current system assessment)
/E (2.2 Current system assessment)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
299 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (There are many challenges facing the NewPoint accounting system used by Al Nahda Foundation, which affect the daily operations. The system is one of the important things that contribute to managing financial transactions and controlling inventory. However, when automation is absent in communicating with suppliers, the process becomes cumbersome and time-consuming. This limitation may reduce the efficiency of the system and cause delays in replenishing essential items.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
