>>
endobj
540 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The operational feasibility of adding an automated supplier communication module to the NewPoint accounting system is high, as it will facilitate supplier interaction and purchasing processes. Manual monitoring and communication, which currently cause delays and errors, will be eliminated. The new system automates monitoring by detecting low stock levels, sending RFQs, and organizing supplier responses into a single portal. This system saves time, reduces human error, and ensures the accuracy of information. Employees can easily compare supplier performance in terms of price and delivery through a central dashboard, speeding up decision-making and strengthening their relationships with suppliers. Automation also allows employees to focus on strategic tasks such as cost analysis and forecasting, improving overall productivity. Additionally, the system provides a clear audit trail, enhancing accountability and transparency. Easily integrated into existing workflows, the solution enables more efficient operations, timely procurement, and fact-based decision-making, enhancing business performance and supplier collaboration in the long run.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
541 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (3.3.2 Technical Feasibility)
/E (3.3.2 Technical Feasibility)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
542 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The technical feasibility of adding an automated supplier communications module to the NewPoint accounting system is highly feasible. Because the system is modular and scalable, new functionality can be added without impacting daily operations or data integrity. The module will connect via secure APIs to receive inventory, supplier, and purchasing data, leveraging existing infrastructure and widely supported technologies, such as automated notifications and dashboards. Integration will be easy with minimal configuration and a reasonable cost, given that the database and servers are already in place. Strong security measures, including encryption and role-based access, will ensure the protection of supplier data. Implementation will be a systematic process involving testing and training to ensure a smooth transition. Maintenance requirements will be minimal, and future enhancements, such as predictive analytics, will be easily added. Overall, this solution is flexible, cost-effective, and technically amenable, enhancing system efficiency and contributing to the company's long-term technological growth.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
